## Database Configuration Details (MySQL)
Configured in `application.properties`:
```properties
server.port=8080
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/arcade_db?createDatabaseIfNotExist=true
spring.datasource.username=root
spring.datasource.password=password
spring.datasource.driver-class-name=com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver

spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
spring.jpa.show-sql=true
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.format_sql=true
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.dialect=org.hibernate.dialect.MySQLDialect

spring.sql.init.mode=always
spring.session.store-type=jdbc
spring.session.jdbc.initialize-schema=always
```

## Complete Spring Boot Code Snippets
*(For the actual submission, you can zip the `src/` folder. Below is the structural representation of the core architecture).*

**1. Model / Entity (`Admin.java`)**
```java
package com.arcade.management.model;
import jakarta.persistence.*;
@Entity
public class Admin {
    @Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;
    private String username;
    private String password;
}
```

**2. Repository (`AdminRepository.java`)**
```java
package com.arcade.management.repository;
import com.arcade.management.model.Admin;
import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.JpaRepository;
public interface AdminRepository extends JpaRepository<Admin, Long> {
    Admin findByUsername(String username);
}
```

**3. Controller**
```java
package com.arcade.management.controller;
// Handles HTTP Requests and delegates to Service
@Controller
@RequestMapping("/players")
public class PlayerController {
    @Autowired
    private PlayerService playerService; // Follows Dependency Inversion Principle
    
    @GetMapping("/login")
    public String showLoginForm() {
        return "players/login"; // Returns Thymeleaf View
    }
}
```

**4. Service implementation (Domain logic / Information Expert)**
```java
package com.arcade.management.service.impl;
@Service
public class PlayerServiceImpl implements PlayerService {
    @Autowired private PlayerRepository playerRepository;
    @Autowired private RankRepository rankRepository;
    
    public void checkAndUpdateRank(Player player) {
        // Business logic to update rank based on score differences
    }
}
```
